 This gem depends on some private git repositories and it is not meant to be used by third parties. But we hope it can serve as inspiration for anyone wanting to run fizzy on their own infrastructure.
 
+## Attachment storage usage
+
+After upgrading an existing database to include `storage_usages`, run
+`bin/rails storage_usage:rebuild` once with the job workers running. This queues
+an idempotent backfill per account. New attachments and account imports update
+the subtotals automatically. `Board#bytes_used` and `Account#bytes_used` reflect
+committed changes once the corresponding jobs finish.
